# Line-ending policy — added 2026-09-03.
#
# Normalization lives HERE, not in each machine's core.autocrlf, because
# several machines and agents commit to this repo. Leaving it to a per-machine
# setting is how 47 .ts/.tsx files reached the index carrying CRLF.
#
# `text=auto` means: git decides text vs binary by content, stores every text
# file with LF in the index, and converts on checkout per platform. Windows
# working copies still get CRLF, so nothing about local editing changes and
# the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" notices on commit are expected, not a fault.
*                text=auto

# DELIBERATELY no per-extension `text` rules. audio_app_archive/ holds ~440
# macOS AppleDouble stubs (._MANIFEST.json, ._BRIEF_AUDIO.md and friends) that
# are binary despite their extensions; a blanket `*.json text` would corrupt
# them. Content detection already classifies them correctly.

# Assets that can never be text, marked explicitly so a new one is never guessed.
*.png            binary
*.PNG            binary
*.jpg            binary
*.jpeg           binary
*.webp           binary
*.gif            binary
*.ico            binary
*.icns           binary
*.ttf            binary
*.otf            binary
*.woff           binary
*.woff2          binary
*.mp3            binary
*.wav            binary
*.m4a            binary
*.aac            binary
*.mp4            binary
*.mov            binary
*.zip            binary
*.pdf            binary
*.xlsx           binary
*.wasm           binary
*.keystore       binary
*.jks            binary
